ing it a truly  harrowing experience  today most viewers know it's not  actually real but the creepiness  persists regardless  watching heather mike and josh lose  themselves in the maryland woods  on the hunt for the blair witch remains  a long and terrifying journey into dread  as the hunters become the hunted heather  reflects on the various mistakes they  made which got them into this awful  predicament  this scene has been parodied to death  and yet it retains its power  heather's desperation is undeniable  making blair witch equal parts sad  and scary plus the ending never fails to  shock as it leaves so much to the  imagination  we never fully learn what actually  happened to the three documentarians  but we can certainly imagine and that  makes it worse  dario argento's moody classic suspiria  is as much an art house movie as it is a  gory descent into the supernatural  suzy banyan is new to her fancy german  dance school but it's not long before  she notices the school has a body count  as suzy uncovers the demonic coven of  witches at the heart of her academy  things go from bad to worse in  increasingly bizarre ways  scored by celebrated prague rock band  goblin the creepy music that wallpaper's  suspiria  adds to susie's mounting dread grotesque  imagery abounds  once you see a woman trapped in a huge  ball of barbed wire  you won't soon forget it add in  argento's close-up camera work  along with the film's vibrant use of  color and you've got a symphony of  horror  sight and sound harmonized to take the  viewer to new heights of fear in  suspiria  one marvels at its beauty even at its  most shocking  being stalked by a serial killer is bad  enough but being stalked by one who  kills people through their dreams is  next level scary  wes craven's a nightmare on elm street  minds that simple premise  brilliantly with an iconic and  terrifying lead character  before he existed in dreams freddy  krueger was a mortal man who preyed on  children  eventually he was killed by a group of  locals when his activities came to light  after they burned him up they vowed  never to speak of him again  years go by in which kruger's spirit  devises the ultimate revenge  he will torment the children of the  people who set him ablaze  although some of these parents are in  denial about his return  but he can't get you now  he's dead honey because mommy killed him  the use of dreams makes nightmare a  movie  still capable of invoking actual  nightmares their lack of logic throws  all the normal rules of horror out the  window  what do you do when the only way to  avoid your monster not sleeping  is physically impossible freddy krueger  is a movie villain unlike any other  and that's what makes this film a spine  tingling classic  in get out photographer chris and his  girlfriend rose have traveled to her  family's estate in upstate new york  chris thinks he is rose's first black  boyfriend but he's dreadfully wrong  the armitage family are actually  murderous racists who transplant the  brains of aging white people  into the bodies of the young healthy  black people they kidnap  the armitage's perfect country home  their manly demeanor  and even their liberal politics are the  cornerstone of director jordan peele's  scathing critique of race in america  but even after chris manages to escape  their clutches  he is confronted with the flashing  lights of a police car  audiences hold their breath wondering if  chris will ever make it home alive  this haunting inn makes get out one of  the scariest movies ever  in a devastating exploration of systemic  bigotry  david fincher's crime horror film 7  follows detectives mills and somerset  during somerset's last week of work the  partners are investigating a serial  killer who is using the seven deadly  sins as his guidebook  fincher's chili aesthetic understates  the horror of each homicide  which actually makes them scarier a  world in which these grotesque deaths  are treated as normal  is a frightening prospect most of the  violence takes place  off-screen which is both blessing and  curse this is a movie that wants viewers  imaginations to go wild  to fill in the blanks and to leave them  with some serious questions  what's in the box seven's ending is also  one of the bleakest of all time  and one of the most unique in being  caught the killer wins  the villain's plan is a master stroke of  horror as is the movie that features him  jaws may be a classic but it has nothing  on the authentic terror of chris  kintus's open water  hardworking couple daniel and susan go  on a tropical vacation to reconnect but  end up getting left behind in the ocean  after their scuba leader miscounts the  people on board the ship  the couple spends hours out in the sea  it's not long before the sharks begin  circling and the two feel their strength  begin to wane  if this premise doesn't scare you on its  own consider this  it's based on a true story watching  daniel and susan struggle to survive as  the sharks get bolder and they grow more  dehydrated is terrifying enough  but to know that two people actually  went through this  that's another level of horror entirely  the ending is as  chilling and hopeless as it is quiet  which makes it unforgettably tragic  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite horror movies are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

